@page "/privacy"

<PageTitle>Privacy notice | Sports Club Hub</PageTitle>

<div class="container">
    <div class="page-header">
        <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
        <p class="lead">What we collect when you register your interest in a sport, and how it is handled.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="panel mb-4">
        <p class="notice">
            This is a plain-language starting point for the demonstration application. Before real use, the organisation
            that operates this service must complete it, appoint an Information Officer and get it reviewed against the
            Protection of Personal Information Act (POPIA).
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-4">What we collect</h2>
        <p>Your name, e-mail address, town or area, an optional phone number, and the sports you are interested in. We also record when you accepted this notice.</p>

        <h2 class="mt-4">Why we collect it</h2>
        <p>To count how many people are interested in each sport in each area, so clubs, venues and municipal sports teams can see where there is demand.</p>

        <h2 class="mt-4">Who can see it</h2>
        <p>Your details are never shown on public pages. Public pages show only totals. Administrators see aggregate statistics and cannot browse individual participants in this application.</p>

        <h2 class="mt-4">What we do not do</h2>
        <p>We do not collect details about children. You must be 18 or older to register. We do not sell your details.</p>

        <h2 class="mt-4">Your choices</h2>
        <p>To see, correct or delete your information, contact the organisation that operates this service: <em>[contact details to be completed by the operator]</em>.</p>
    </div>
</div>
